Experiment 2: Common Elements Between Two Arrays
Aim

To find the common elements between two arrays and analyse its time complexity.

Algorithm
Take each element of the first array.
Compare it with every element of the second array.
If a match is found, print the element and stop searching the second array for it.
Repeat for all elements of the first array.
Pseudo code
CommonElements(A, n, B, m)
  for i = 0 to n-1
      for j = 0 to m-1
          if A[i] == B[j]
              print A[i]
              break
Source code (C)
c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    int a[] = {1, 3, 5, 7, 9};
    int b[] = {3, 6, 9, 12, 5};
    int n = 5, m = 5, i, j, count = 0;

    printf("Common elements: ");
    for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        for (j = 0; j < m; j++) {
            if (a[i] == b[j]) {
                printf("%d ", a[i]);
                count++;
                break;
            }
        }
    }

    if (count == 0)
        printf("None");
    printf("\n");

    return 0;
}
Output
Common elements: 3 5 9
Result

The common elements between the two arrays were found as 3, 5 and 9.

Time complexity: O(n × m), or O(n²) when both arrays have the same size, because of the nested loops.
Space complexity: O(1).
